edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316977 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316977 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186316977 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b78a1356-a5af-5e99-a19b-ab124b5e015e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186315362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317048 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317048 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317048 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186315362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317048 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d44aeb71-27ee-5525-8a16-85847bd3372c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317065 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186316196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317065 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317065 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317065 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186316196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317065 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "da42b32b-84df-5fb0-a246-7c6e69f97114" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316698 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1069 "q-341994" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1071 "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.4$ | $1.1$ | $3.7$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ad24a5a-c3d4-5218-8b93-0b9b0b21bc08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317191 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.6) & ≈\\frac{g(0.6+0.3)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0.9)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.1-(-0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.3} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316579 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342003" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1071 "A function $d(y)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $d(y)$ | $-8.92$ | $-11.34$ | $-15.23$ | $-17.56$ | $-18.21$ | $-18.50$ |\n\nApproximate ${d}^{′}(y)$ at the point $y=-5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${d}^{′}(-5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2776278-e397-5818-9d00-bb84155b42d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317193 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{d}^{′}(y)≈\\frac{d(y+h)-d(y)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $y=-5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(-5) & ≈\\frac{d(-5+2)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{d(-3)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11.34-(-8.92)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.42}{2} \\\\  & =-1.21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186316977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342075" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d8/d84ba0a07821011be4cf5958af44ea73e97493c5a796a0324b068fe2adca8a12.png)\n\nA car is using petrol as it travels. The graph of the amount of petrol $P(d)$, in liters, remaining in the fuel tank after traveling a distance of $d$ miles is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the amount of petrol at $d=150$ using a forward difference with step size $h=50.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the amount of petrol decreases.\n\nAfter traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is {{field-1}} liters per mile." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22176dc8-13fa-5e60-9e3c-ce6a132e5f6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317204 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(d)≈\\frac{P(d+h)-P(d)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the distance $d=150$ with step size $h=50.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(150) & ≈\\frac{P(150+50)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(200)-P(150)}{50} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-30}{50} \\\\  & =-0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after traveling $150$ miles, the rate of change of the amount of petrol is $-0.4$ liters per mile." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186317048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342079" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/84/846fc347c71ada4c01a5a85aabd0722203b84edbafcbe462064ae31d1cf2adbb.png)\n\nA drone is descending toward the ground. The graph of its height $H(t)$, in meters, after $t$ minutes is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the height at $t=9$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the height decreases.\n\nAfter $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is {{field-1}} meters per minute." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fc754b10-9417-5d37-9ac6-29d601a462cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317205 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{H}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{H(t+h)-H(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=9$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{′}(9) & ≈\\frac{H(9+2)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{H(11)-H(9)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{0-80}{2} \\\\  & =-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $9$ minutes, the rate of change of the height is $-40$ meters per minute." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186317065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1069 "q-342080" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ae/ae57faa04abd053e4a58d751cc084d58e07e84e0520c99a33a122f58dfd8f18c.png)\n\nA slice of jackfruit is placed in an air dryer. The graph of the moisture content $M(t)$, in percent, after $t$ hours is shown above. Approximate the rate of change of the moisture content at $t=3$ using a forward difference with step size $h=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n*Hint*: Assume that the rate of change is negative if the content decreases.\n\nAfter $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is {{field-1}} percent per hour." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "870839f6-6361-5527-8457-2d1a8f03542c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186317206 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{M(t+h)-M(t)}{h},\n$$\n\nat the time $t=3$ with step size $h=2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{M(3+2)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{M(5)-M(3)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{20-40}{2} \\\\  & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, after $3$ hour, the rate of change of moisture content is $-10$ percent per hour." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327103 #edb/ref 1080 "-0.6\\,\\text{liters/mile}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327103 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327103 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "13cc7f8a-6ea7-5664-b228-b75e01609825" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327446 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186327446 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175